# DB state after the fleet's hour: every table of the schema.
#
# The hour:   the call-plan fleet of 5 fake devices (callplan_harness_test.go), every scheduled loop,
#             one simulated hour and a minute from 2026-01-05 12:00 UTC; the devices' counters, CPU,
#             memory and uptime move with the clock (callplan_motion_test.go)
#
# A change in this file is a change in what the pollers store.
# Rewrite it with: go test ./internal/poller -run TestDBState -update

## Written in the hour: one golden file each

bridge_port_status          99 rows  NetworkHealthPoller.readBridges → queries.UpsertBridgePortStatus (stale rows: NetworkHealthPoller.maintain → queries.DeleteStaleBridgeRows)
bridge_status                5 rows  NetworkHealthPoller.readBridges → queries.UpsertBridgeStatus (stale rows: NetworkHealthPoller.maintain → queries.DeleteStaleBridgeRows)
bridge_vlans                13 rows  NetworkHealthPoller.readVLANs → queries.UpsertBridgeVLAN (stale rows: NetworkHealthPoller.maintain → queries.DeleteStaleBridgeVLANs)
client_history              43 rows  ClientDiscoveryPoller.store → ingest.Sink.Emit → ingest.ApplyClientSeen → queries.InsertClientHistory
client_signal_samples      122 rows  ConnectivityPoller.collectSignals → queries.InsertClientSignalSample
device_audit                 5 rows  Auditor.storeSnapshot → queries.InsertDeviceAudit
device_audit_runs            5 rows  Auditor.begin → queries.InsertAuditRun
                                     Auditor.finish → queries.FinishAuditRun
device_findings              4 rows  Auditor.storeFindings → queries.UpsertAuditFinding (and DeleteAuditFindingsExcept, ReleaseAuditFindings for what a pass no longer sees)
device_hours                 5 rows  PortStatsCollector.flush → queries.RollupDeviceHours (when the flush crosses an hour; PortStatsCollector.startupRollup at the start)
device_minutes             300 rows  LoadRecorder.FlushMinutes (the port-stats collector's CoverageSink, from PortStatsCollector.flush) → queries.UpsertDeviceMinutes; fed by the collector's Tier 0 coverage, Manager.pollDevice → LoadRecorder.NoteLiveness, CPUSampler.sample / samplePost → LoadRecorder.AddSample / AddPostSample, and the routeros observer → LoadRecorder.Command / Session
device_uplinks               5 rows  Manager.collectUplinks → queries.ReplaceDeviceUplinks (gateway-host rows: Manager.resolveGatewayHosts → queries.ReplaceGatewayHosts)
devices                      5 rows  Manager.pollDevice (liveness) → queries.MarkDeviceOnline: status, last_seen, last_error
                                     Manager.refreshDeviceInfo (Tier 6) → queries.UpdateDeviceHealth: cpu_load, memory, uptime, last_seen; queries.UpdateDeviceInfo: platform, board, ros_version, firmware_version, architecture
                                     Manager.probeClass → queries.SetDeviceClass: device_class, class_probed_at, cpu_count, cpu_mhz_max
                                     CPUSampler.sample (Tier 1) → queries.UpdateDeviceLoad: cpu_load, memory_used, uptime
firmware_status              5 rows  Manager.refreshDeviceInfo (Tier 6) → FirmwareChecker.RecordDevice → queries.UpsertDeviceFirmware
interface_relations          6 rows  PortStatsCollector.collectDeviceRelations (Tier 3c) → queries.ReplaceInterfaceRelations
interface_state            109 rows  NetworkHealthPoller.monitorPorts → queries.UpsertInterfaceState (stale rows: NetworkHealthPoller.maintain → queries.DeleteStaleInterfaceStates)
interfaces                 113 rows  PortStatsCollector.syncInventory (Tier 0) → queries.SyncInterfaces
links                        4 rows  Manager.pollTopology → topology.Builder.Build → queries.UpsertLink (MarkStaleLinksDown, DeleteOldLinks)
mac_lookup                   9 rows  ClientDiscoveryPoller.store → ingest.Sink.Emit → ingest.ApplyClientSeen → queries.UpsertMACLookup
                                     WifiTracker.poll → queries.UpsertMACLookup
neighbors                    8 rows  Manager.collectNeighbors (Tier 3d) → queries.UpsertNeighbor (stale rows: Manager.sweepNeighbors)
ping_samples               244 rows  ConnectivityPoller.persistAndPublish → queries.InsertPingSample
ping_targets                 2 rows  ConnectivityPoller.poll → queries.UpdatePingTargetAddress: a client watch's address
port_hosts                 127 rows  PortStatsCollector.collectDeviceHosts (Tier 3b) → queries.UpsertPortHosts
port_stats_1h               64 rows  PortStatsCollector.flush → queries.RollupPortStats1h (when the flush crosses an hour; PortStatsCollector.startupRollup at the start)
port_stats_1m             3840 rows  PortStatsCollector.flush → queries.InsertPortStats1m
wifi_history                 5 rows  WifiTracker.emitFromSnapshot / handleLogEvent / emitLeave → queries.InsertWifiHistory

## Filled before the hour, not written in it (checked unchanged)

app_settings                32 rows  the migrations' defaults and NewManager's AdoptIntervalSettings, before the hour; the loops only read it
goose_db_version            35 rows  the migrations

## Empty after the hour

alert_silences           written only by the API (an admin's silence)
alerts                   the alert engine is not part of the hour (Manager.Start runs it; it reads only the database)
audit_log                the API's admin actions, and Manager.probeClass when a class change is accepted — the hour's probes agree with the stored classes
device_address_proposals IP auto-follow (auto_follow_ip) is off, and no device is heard at another address
dns_servers              written only by the API (settings)
firmware_releases        the release feed (FirmwareChecker.fetch) is not part of the hour: it reads the internet, not a device
flow_1h                  the flow collector is not part of the hour (off unless MIKROTIK_NMS_FLOW_LISTEN is set)
flow_1h_meta             the flow collector is not part of the hour
flow_1m                  the flow collector is not part of the hour
flow_1m_meta             the flow collector is not part of the hour
flow_export_checks       the flow collector is not part of the hour
flow_export_watches      the flow collector is not part of the hour (a watch starts when it accepts an exporter)
flow_exporter_ifaces     the flow collector is not part of the hour
flow_exporters           the flow collector is not part of the hour, and an exporter is added by an admin
flow_points              the flow collector is not part of the hour
flow_prefixes            the flow collector is not part of the hour
flow_sender_policy       the flow collector is not part of the hour
flow_templates           the flow collector is not part of the hour
loop_events              network health records a loop, a MAC flap, a port going down, flapping or disabled, or an address move: none happens in the hour
map_positions            written only by the API (an admin's saved map layout)
notification_channels    written only by the API
password_reset_tokens    written only by the API
speed_samples            the speed-test loop is not part of the hour, and no test is configured
speed_tests              written only by the API
traceroute_runs          a traceroute is captured on demand, or when an internet target loses at least traceroute_loss_threshold (off by default): every probe of the hour is answered
traffic_samples          the on-demand live stream (TrafficManager) is not part of the hour: nobody subscribes
upgrade_job_devices      firmware upgrades are an admin's action
upgrade_jobs             firmware upgrades are an admin's action
users                    the harness logs nobody in; only the API writes users
vlan_labels              written only by the API (an admin's labels)

## SQLite's own

sqlite_sequence          SQLite's AUTOINCREMENT counters, which follow the tables above

## Times from the wall clock (wallClockColumns), checked against the values: what v2 ingest
## semantics (an observed_at carried from the read) changes

bridge_port_status.last_polled     SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)
bridge_status.last_polled          SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)
bridge_vlans.last_polled           SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)
client_history.recorded_at         SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)
device_uplinks.last_seen           SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)
devices.last_seen                  SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)
devices.updated_at                 SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)
firmware_status.last_checked       SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)
firmware_status.updated_at         SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)
interface_relations.updated_at     SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)
interface_state.last_polled        SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)
interfaces.last_updated            SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)
links.last_seen                    SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)
mac_lookup.updated_at              SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)
neighbors.last_seen                SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)
ping_samples.recorded_at           time.Now() in Go (wall clock)
wifi_history.recorded_at           SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock)

## Columns of the tables the hour leaves empty whose default is the wall clock (the schema's)

audit_log.at                       DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
dns_servers.created_at             DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
flow_exporters.created_at          DEFAULT CAST(strftime('%s','now') AS INTEGER)
flow_points.created_at             DEFAULT CAST(strftime('%s','now') AS INTEGER)
loop_events.recorded_at            DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
password_reset_tokens.created_at   DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
speed_samples.recorded_at          DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
speed_tests.created_at             DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
traceroute_runs.recorded_at        DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
traffic_samples.collected_at       DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
upgrade_jobs.created_at            DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
users.created_at                   DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
vlan_labels.updated_at             DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
